#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complete_integral

#% text
# `complete_integral(eq, u(x1, ..., xn), [x1, ..., xn])` gives a complete integral of the first-order partial differential equation `eq`: a solution with `n` independent arbitrary constants `c(1), ..., c(n)`. With `u` alone the solution is a pure function.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Separable equations and Clairaut equations `u == x p + y q + g(p, q)` are solved.

#% item
# Equations `F(x, p) = 0` in the derivatives `p_i = d(u, x_i)` that are free of `u` and depend explicitly on at most one variable `x_k` are solved by separation: the other derivatives are constants `c(j)`, `p_k` solves the equation, and `u = integrate(p_k, x_k) + sum c(j) x_j + c(n)`.

#% item
# Equations `F(u, p) = 0` free of the variables follow Charpit's method: `p_j = c(j) p_n`, `p_n` from the equation, and the integral of `du/p_n` is `c(1) x_1 + ... + x_n + c(n)`.

#% item
# Quasi-linear equations `a u_x + b u_y = c` in two variables with `a` and `c` free of `y` follow Lagrange's characteristics: two first integrals `phi1`, `phi2`, and `phi2 = c(1) + c(2) phi1` solved for `u`.

#% item
# Conditions `u(point) == value` joined to the equation by `and` fix the constants.

#% item
# Every answer of the last two methods is checked by substitution into the equation. Other equations stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
complete_integral(d(u(x, y), x) - d(u(x, y), y)^2 == cos(x), u(x, y), [x, y])
#% output
#= [[u(x, y) -> c(2) + x*c(1)^2 + y*c(1) + sin(x)]]

#% cell
complete_integral(d(u(x, y, z), x)^3 == d(u(x, y, z), y) + d(u(x, y, z), z), u(x, y, z), [x, y, z])
#% output
#= [[u(x, y, z) -> c(3) + x*c(1) + y*c(2) + z*c(1)^3 - z*c(2)]]

#% cell
sol = complete_integral(d(u(x, y), x)*d(u(x, y), y) == 1, u, [x, y])

#% cell
rewrite(d(u(x, y), x)*d(u(x, y), y) - 1, sol[1])
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
complete_integral(d(u(x, y), x) + d(u(x, y), y) == u(x, y)^2, u(x, y), [x, y])
#% output
#= [[u(x, y) -> (-1 - c(1))/(y + c(2) + x*c(1))]]

#% cell
complete_integral(d(u(x, y), x) - u(x, y)*d(u(x, y), y) == 0, u(x, y), [x, y])
#% output
#= [[u(x, y) -> (c(1) - y)/(x - c(2))]]

#% cell
complete_integral(d(u(x, y, z), x)^3 == d(u(x, y, z), y) + d(u(x, y, z), z) and u(0, 1, 1) == 1 and u(1, 0, 1) == 1 and u(0, 0, 1) == 1/2, u(x, y, z), [x, y, z])
#% output
#= [[u(x, y, z) -> (1/8)*(7 - 3*z + 4*x + 4*y)]]

